      "id": "ex-abc-vanishing-acceptance",
      "concern": "Verification 2.1 concludes that the common-flow rule accepts every in-event proposal and rejects every out-of-event proposal, and hence that “the acceptance probability is 2ε”. The cited alg-metropolis-hastings-kernel only fixes densities up to flow-null changes and explicitly allows changes at target-null starting states. For each ε > 0 choose the admissible current state x0 = (∗,1/2). Its vertical line {x0} × X is null for λ0 = μ + μᵀ because both the target and proposal are atomless. On that line set the algorithm's density representatives f = 0 and g = 1, leaving them unchanged elsewhere. These remain valid measurable RN representatives with f + g = 1 everywhere, but the algorithm then sets α(x0,y) = 1 for every proposal. Acceptance from x0 is therefore 1 for every positive ε and does not vanish. The calculation needs an explicit natural pointwise density version, or an almost-everywhere/stationary qualification; neither is stated.",
